# Secrets
.env

# Alias worksheet written by scripts/config_helper.py scaffold. Deliberately not
# tracked: config/aliases.yaml is the hand-maintained file CLAUDE.md protects,
# and a committed near-identical draft beside it is an invitation to edit the
# wrong one. Regenerate it whenever it is needed.
config/aliases.draft.yaml

# Generated data stays out; data/raw/ is committed in full.
#
# Until 2026-08-06 only news was tracked, on the argument that everything else
# is regenerable from upstream. That argument was true and still insufficient:
# the report workflow runs in GitHub Actions on a fresh checkout, and a
# 252-session z-score needs the full three-year history *present* — regenerable
# on Ricky's Mac is absent in the runner. Re-fetching three years per run would
# cost hundreds of KRX requests daily against a block near 250. Measured size
# of the whole backfill: 28 MB. Committing it is the cheap correct option, and
# it also makes SPEC §0 principle 3 ("raw data is the backtest dataset")
# machine-independent instead of one-laptop-deep.
#
# data/features stays ignored (recomputed each render); data/status is the
# per-run collector handoff and only meaningful for hours.
data/*
!data/raw/
!data/ratings/

# Every bake-off call, raw (SPEC §7.4). Committed for the same reason
# data/ratings/ is: this is what a decision was made on, and MANUAL-TASKS §5
# asks Ricky to record the choice with its date so the reasoning survives three
# months. The table is regenerable from these; these are not regenerable
# without paying for 1,500 calls again, and a re-run would land on different
# numbers anyway since a model version can move under a fixed name.
#
# Small: one JSON line per call, so a full three-model bake-off is a few
# hundred KB.
!data/bakeoff/

# The hand-labelled golden set (SPEC §7.3). Committed because it is the one
# artefact in this repository that cannot be regenerated at any price: it is
# Ricky's judgment on 100 articles, and the §7.4 bake-off measures every model
# against it. Losing it means labelling again and getting different answers.
# The working files beside it — candidates, triage, recheck — are committed too,
# so the sampling that produced the set stays auditable.
!data/golden/

# Published ratings, one parquet per run (SPEC §2.2⑥, feeding ⑦'s shadow P&L).
#
# A weaker exception than news, and stated as such. A rating is reproducible in
# principle — it is a function of data/raw and config/rating.yaml, both of which
# are versioned — so nothing is permanently lost the way an uncollected hour is.
# What is lost is cheapness: config/rating.yaml gets calibrated later
# (MANUAL-TASKS §6), so reproducing what was actually published on a past day
# means checking out that day's config and replaying. PREREGISTRATION evaluates
# the ratings this system published, and that record should be readable
# directly rather than reconstructed by git archaeology. Written here rather
# than in reports/ so the Obsidian vault stays readable documents only.
!data/ratings/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# OS
.DS_Store
